      2  3100							;
      3  3100							; The playfield of the 16 rooms (bank3.asm, from
      4  3100							; dungeon.py): 60 bytes each, the order of the Superchip
      5  3100							; RAM (PF0 of the 20 courses, then PF1, then PF2), with the
      6  3100							; grate closed and the plates of the spikes down.
      7  3100							; Bank 7 calls room_copy with jsr TO_COPY when Sir Roderick
      8  3100							; comes into a room; the trampoline in the tail of every
      9  3100							; bank brings it here and takes it back.
     10  3100
     11  3100							; room_copy: the playfield of room `room` into the Superchip
     12  3100							; RAM, from the last byte down. The change of room is the
     13  3100							; heaviest frame of the VBLANK, so the loop is unrolled:
     14  3100							; 60 copies of the three instructions, 12 cycles a byte
     15  3100							; (13 when the load crosses a page) instead of 15 or 16.
     16  3100				   room_copy
